{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1021914-so-solars-can-t-speak-with-animals-anymore","id":1021914,"title":"So solars can't speak with animals anymore?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-25T03:07:55-08:00","id":1021914,"title":"So solars can't speak with animals anymore?","content":"So I'm noticing Friendship with Animals Approach no longer allows a Solar to speak with animals anymore. In a way I may enjoy this if this means Lunars will be better at speaking with animals then Solars. But being as it currently stands does this mean Sorcerous Workings are the current method to allow Solars to speak with Animals?<br /> <br /> Am I missing something? We were having a Solar learn Friendship with Animals Approach but if it doesn't allow beast speech she doesn't want to learn it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T03:09:44-08:00","id":1021915,"title":"","content":"The solar charm list is non-exhaustive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T03:11:44-08:00","id":1021917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1021914-so-solars-can-t-speak-with-animals-anymore?p=1021915#post1021915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The solar charm list is non-exhaustive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes but Friendship with Animals Approach used to be the charm that lets you speak with animals...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T03:12:34-08:00","id":1021918,"title":"","content":"Well, now it's the <i>prerequisite.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T03:40:56-08:00","id":1021924,"title":"","content":"Did it actually let you speak with animals? Or just let you make social attacks on them?<br /> <br /> Honestly, I think it's fine if Lunars are the only ones who can actually have a proper conversation with animals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T04:11:47-08:00","id":1021929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1021914-so-solars-can-t-speak-with-animals-anymore?p=1021924#post1021924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did it actually let you speak with animals? Or just let you make social attacks on them?</div> </div> </div> </div>The EX2 charm allowed the Exalt to communicate with the animal, through sounds and gestures, as though they shared a common language; although it noted that they had limited comprehension.<br /> <br /> EX3 dropped this, and simply makes animals more approachable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T16:25:18-08:00","id":1022124,"title":"","content":"I question what animals have to say.<br /> <br /> \u200bI really doubt that it was on anybody's mind when rewriting the Charm, but recently I've faced certain lines of discussion that leave me to feel as though a general ability to talk to mundane animals asks all kinds of odd questions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T16:32:59-08:00","id":1022129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1021914-so-solars-can-t-speak-with-animals-anymore?p=1022124#post1022124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I question what animals have to say.<br /> <br /> \u200bI really doubt that it was on anybody's mind when rewriting the Charm, but recently I've faced certain lines of discussion that leave me to feel as though a general ability to talk to mundane animals asks all kinds of odd questions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I expressed something similar when he asked this question in &quot;Ask a Question,&quot; but I'd like to hear your side more, if you wouldn't mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T17:29:13-08:00","id":1022144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1021914-so-solars-can-t-speak-with-animals-anymore?p=1021924#post1021924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did it actually let you speak with animals? Or just let you make social attacks on them?<br /> <br /> Honestly, I think it's fine if Lunars are the only ones who can actually have a proper conversation with animals.</div> </div> </div> </div>You just need to learn the universal language of birds <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12796-beast-of-bitter-oblivion","name":"Beast of Bitter Oblivion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12796_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T17:37:15-08:00","id":1022148,"title":"","content":"Mostly it's a matter of the question of whether an animal being able to communicate with a human in the least bit comprehensible way implies that it is sapient, at least in a manner sufficiently similar to humans.<br /> <br /> \u200bMind, it also relates to some things I've read about the cognitive and neurological evolution of language in humans, and how this relates to observed or speculated behaviours even in animals that appear to be capable of communication.<br /> <br /> \u200bFor instance, the chain of logic relating matters of the capacity to conceive abstract concepts, or even possess mental images of things that are not currently present, to the matter of how the capacity of language to describe something that is not currently present requiring sufficiently developed neurology to be capable of something like trust, and how this also necessarily entails the capacity to lie. Indeed, it appears that a cognitive capacity for trust and living up to that trust is a necessity for abstract language to be sustained by evolution, otherwise something akin to lying would have had an excessive advantage that would have placed an intolerable survival burden on language.<br /> <br /> \u200bOr something to that effect; it's probably a crude and half-remembered version of what I actually read, so some of the specifics are off, but I think it conveys the basic idea that the capacity for language is extremely biologically sophisticated.<br /> <br /> \u200bI mean jeez, just think of how many words I'm using in this sentence alone that convey concepts that do not objectively exist.<br /> <br /> \u200bI know Exalted is a fantasy setting, but even by the standards of fantasy these are questions that I just wouldn't be able to ignore, because the matter of talking to an animal that still acts like an animal has become something I can hardly suspend my disbelief for.<br /> <br /> \u200b(And the idea of magic that makes animals able to speak only within the boundaries of the use of the magic is just too fiddly for me to tolerate)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T17:55:49-08:00","id":1022158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1021914-so-solars-can-t-speak-with-animals-anymore?p=1022148#post1022148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mostly it's a matter of the question of whether an animal being able to communicate with a human in the least bit comprehensible way implies that it is sapient, at least in a manner sufficiently similar to humans.<br /> <br /> \u200bMind, it also relates to some things I've read about the cognitive and neurological evolution of language in humans, and how this relates to observed or speculated behaviours even in animals that appear to be capable of communication.<br /> <br /> \u200bFor instance, the chain of logic relating matters of the capacity to conceive abstract concepts, or even possess mental images of things that are not currently present, to the matter of how the capacity of language to describe something that is not currently present requiring sufficiently developed neurology to be capable of something like trust, and how this also necessarily entails the capacity to lie. Indeed, it appears that a cognitive capacity for trust and living up to that trust is a necessity for abstract language to be sustained by evolution, otherwise something akin to lying would have had an excessive advantage that would have placed an intolerable survival burden on language.<br /> <br /> \u200bOr something to that effect; it's probably a crude and half-remembered version of what I actually read, so some of the specifics are off, but I think it conveys the basic idea that the capacity for language is extremely biologically sophisticated.<br /> <br /> \u200bI mean jeez, just think of how many words I'm using in this sentence alone that convey concepts that do not objectively exist.<br /> <br /> \u200bI know Exalted is a fantasy setting, but even by the standards of fantasy these are questions that I just wouldn't be able to ignore, because the matter of talking to an animal that still acts like an animal has become something I can hardly suspend my disbelief for.<br /> <br /> \u200b(And the idea of magic that makes animals able to speak only within the boundaries of the use of the magic is just too fiddly for me to tolerate)</div> </div> </div> </div>I would imagine, <u>at best,</u> that it would be kinda like talking to a 3-year-old child that has very little understanding of the actual concepts you want to talk about. At that would be with the more &quot;intelligent&quot; animals, like corvids, cetaceans, etc.<br /> <br /> Solar: So, hey there bird. Did you see any Dragonblooded coming up from the south?<br /> Raven: I'M HUNGRY.<br /> Solar: What? Come on, answer my question.<br /> Raven: FEED ME. WHATS &quot;SOUTH&quot;? WHAT ARE &quot;DRAGONBLOODED&quot;. FEEEEEEEEEEEDDD MEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEE<br /> Solar: Fuck this.<br /> <br /> Just because you can &quot;talk&quot; to animals doesn't mean they are going to understand what the hell you are talking about. Hell, this happens with humans from different parts of the globe. An Inuit might have 30 different words to describe different types of snow, but that doesn't mean they are going to know about tropical islands.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11892-boston123","name":"Boston123","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T18:40:32-08:00","id":1022163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Boston123</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1021914-so-solars-can-t-speak-with-animals-anymore?p=1022158#post1022158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hell, this happens with humans from different parts of the globe. An Inuit might have 30 different words to describe different types of snow, but that doesn't mean they are going to know about tropical islands.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI don't think those are quite the same, for reasons including the aforementioned capacity to form abstract images, and especially in any cases in which different people are sharing ideas.<br /> <br /> \u200bA given person might not understand a given word, what with the also aforementioned fact of how words aren't really objective things and are only functional on account of being socialised to associate them with relevant images, but sufficient conversation can probably get somebody without a specific disorder from getting there.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe terms I'm talking about are even more fundamental than an animal not understanding what you're talking about, it's more like not having the capacity to form things like questions in the first place.<br /> <br /> I don't want to harp on about this, just try to clarify my own position.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T18:57:37-08:00","id":1022167,"title":"","content":"You're not wrong, Isator, but my big objection to it was a little more rooted in how it changes the role of mundane animals in one's game. Even with riders about animals not understanding abstractions and such, the Charm turns animals into repositories of knowledge, and there may not be an ST clever enough to keep vital plot information secret from a clever player with access to the entirety of Kingdom <i>Animalia</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T22:05:27-08:00","id":1022226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beast of Bitter Oblivion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1021914-so-solars-can-t-speak-with-animals-anymore?p=1022144#post1022144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You just need to learn the universal language of birds <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm thinking Flat Earth and i&quot;m reminded that birds are especially dumb and crazy by human standards.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T23:02:12-08:00","id":1022233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Boston123</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1021914-so-solars-can-t-speak-with-animals-anymore?p=1022158#post1022158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would imagine, <u>at best,</u> that it would be kinda like talking to a 3-year-old child that has very little understanding of the actual concepts you want to talk about. At that would be with the more &quot;intelligent&quot; animals, like corvids, cetaceans, etc.<br /> <br /> Solar: So, hey there bird. Did you see any Dragonblooded coming up from the south?<br /> Raven: I'M HUNGRY.<br /> Solar: What? Come on, answer my question.<br /> Raven: FEED ME. WHATS &quot;SOUTH&quot;? WHAT ARE &quot;DRAGONBLOODED&quot;. FEEEEEEEEEEEDDD MEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEE<br /> Solar: Fuck this.<br /> <br /> Just because you can &quot;talk&quot; to animals doesn't mean they are going to understand what the hell you are talking about. Hell, this happens with humans from different parts of the globe. An Inuit might have 30 different words to describe different types of snow, but that doesn't mean they are going to know about tropical islands.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, certain bird-species would probably be your best bet. Especially corvids, who tend to be unwholesomely intelligent.<br /> <br /> The amercian crow, for example, is capable of distinguishing different humans based on our facial features; more importantly, they are capable of describing our appearance to other crows with enough fidelity that they can recognize us. If you bother one crow, it can tell all the other crows and they'll remember and dislike you for literally generations.<br /> <br /> Crows are capable of intergenerational grudges! It's really neat.<br /> <br /> So I don't doubt that you could describe the dragonblooded hunting you in great detail, state emphatically that they're hunting you down to try and kill you, and then the crows would be more than happy to warn you. Or, at least, be on the look-out and warn each other, which you'd hear because you can talk to crows for some reason.<br /> <br /> Some species of Corvids are about as smart as Great Apes!<br /> A lot of other birds are kind of dumb though, so, it's one of those good-bad things! But as far as birds go, Ravens and Crows and other Corvids are a pretty good bet on facial-recognition and problem solving metrics!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4578-zale","name":"Zale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4578_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T03:00:31-08:00","id":1022255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beast of Bitter Oblivion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1021914-so-solars-can-t-speak-with-animals-anymore?p=1022144#post1022144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You just need to learn the universal language of birds <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>AAAAAARRRGHHHH! Stupid fucking universal fucking language of birds...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T03:06:20-08:00","id":1022257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Boston123</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1021914-so-solars-can-t-speak-with-animals-anymore?p=1022158#post1022158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would imagine, <u>at best,</u> that it would be kinda like talking to a 3-year-old child that has very little understanding of the actual concepts you want to talk about. At that would be with the more &quot;intelligent&quot; animals, like corvids, cetaceans, etc.<br /> <br /> Solar: So, hey there bird. Did you see any Dragonblooded coming up from the south?<br /> Raven: I'M HUNGRY.<br /> Solar: What? Come on, answer my question.<br /> Raven: FEED ME. WHATS &quot;SOUTH&quot;? WHAT ARE &quot;DRAGONBLOODED&quot;. FEEEEEEEEEEEDDD MEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEE<br /> Solar: Fuck this.<br /> <br /> Just because you can &quot;talk&quot; to animals doesn't mean they are going to understand what the hell you are talking about. Hell, this happens with humans from different parts of the globe. An Inuit might have 30 different words to describe different types of snow, but that doesn't mean they are going to know about tropical islands.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is how I always ran it with Lunars (or, for that matter, Animalism in Vampire). Lunars can ask say, some horses if they saw a thief... but horses don't understand what a thief is (or know how to recognise it). So they try and describe a man who was wearing a red shirt and a black hat... and the horses don't remember, and don't know what a shirt or hat is. The only people they actually can recognise is their regular rider.<br /> <br /> Which, I think, deals with your worry Alucard. Some animals might have useful info for Lunars to discover, but it's likely to be fragmentary and specific, and most animals won't because they're just too stupid.<br /> <br /> That always worked fine, and, honestly, was generally a lot of fun to roleplay!<br /> <br /> (I still don't think Solars should be able to talk to/understand animals. Command them with body language like a human can sometimes do, sure, but not have a conversation with them, even if it's a conversation where the animal just says &quot;Food?&quot; over and over again.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 12-26-2016, 09:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T05:43:24-08:00","id":1022285,"title":"","content":"Honestly I'm divided on the subject, on the one hand I can't see any thematic reason why Solars shouldn't, the other issues mentioned with people being able to use every animal as a source of information with only a single Charm, are certainly good reasons though.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, talking with animals also seems like a Lunar <i>thing</i> to me (but that also might be me being stuck in an outdated mindset, because 3e aims to try and correct the mistakes of the past.. just like the Exalted... oh shit, we're doomed!), so we might see that come into the game anyway, probably limited only to those animals that the Lunar can transform into.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1021914-so-solars-can-t-speak-with-animals-anymore?p=1022233#post1022233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Crows are capable of intergenerational grudges! It's really neat.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually learned rather recently that crows and owls absolutely HATE each other, and have been seen to go out of their way to attack each other for no reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12167-broken-masque","name":"Broken Masque","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T06:10:42-08:00","id":1022292,"title":"","content":"It's not for<i> no </i>reason, it's just not for a reason we understand.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T06:49:26-08:00","id":1022306,"title":"","content":"I think being able to communicate with animals needs sufficient space to explain the limitations of doing that, otherwise it's going to offer enormous unintended advantages or be a useless power that's going to consist of being stonewalled by the ST trying to portray an alien mindset.<br /> <br /> I suspect Lunars will set a few precedents there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T07:05:38-08:00","id":1022311,"title":"","content":"If you are gonna have a folk/myth hero with the ability to speak with animals, I don't think &quot;hur hur, you can't get anything out of it because animals are dumb&quot; should be a big limitation.<br /> <br /> As for Solars, I think they should go up to Disney Princess. You know, have animals understand them and collaborate with them, try to cheer them up or just be helpful in general, but not hold a conversation.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Actually... <b>Maybe </b>as one of those really unusual multi-Ability Charms, I might allow one with the Disney Princess survival Charm and the voice imitation Performance stuff to develop an animal conversation Charm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":868,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","user":"danelsan","date":". 12-26-2016, 01:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T08:11:02-08:00","id":1022344,"title":"","content":"In the real world sure, the absolute best the animal kingdom has to offer is a captive gorilla who can communicate with about as much complexity as a kindergartener via sign language. But there are all kinds of myths and folk tales that involve people having conversations with woodland animals who seem quite intelligent and sapient, while having no particular special magical reason for being so. I don't know that this is an area I'd want to be a stickler for verisimilitude in while otherwise dealing with gods, demons, storm spirits that freak out over women on ships, heroes that can split a boulder with an axe blow, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T08:29:53-08:00","id":1022352,"title":"","content":"Eh... I think it's reasonable for those to be animal <i>gods </i>(or god-bloods), and then regular animals have the intelligence, of, well, animals. I mean, I do see what you mean, genre-wise, but I think it's easier to split it that way, otherwise you wonder about the actions of animals if they're all that intelligent.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for Solars, I think they should go up to Disney Princess. You know, have animals understand them and collaborate with them, try to cheer them up or just be helpful in general, but not hold a conversation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I agree. Having actual conversations with animals seems the sort of explicit-supernatural-and-animal-themed thing that's out of theme for Solars, but in-theme for Lunars.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Broken Masque</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the other hand, talking with animals also seems like a Lunar <i>thing</i> to me (but that also might be me being stuck in an outdated mindset, because 3e aims to try and correct the mistakes of the past.. just like the Exalted... oh shit, we're doomed!), so we might see that come into the game anyway, probably limited only to those animals that the Lunar can transform into.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering that talking to any animal was literally the easiest charm for Lunars to acquire in 2e*, and that never broke anything, it would seem rather restrictive to make it only the animals that Lunars can turn into.<br /> (Was a bit pricey though, at 1m, 1wp, but there was a discount to 1m if you were using it to talk to the same kind of animal as you were in the form of.)<br /> <br /> *Essence 1, no prereq charms, Attribute 1, and favoured for both Charisma and Perception","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 12-26-2016, 11:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T08:51:41-08:00","id":1022359,"title":"","content":"I think to square the circle of animal action with selective humanlike intelligence capabilities, it probably moves you to an interesting view of animal nature where they do what they do apparently unintelligent and irrational actions because of overpowering instincts and drives, rather than a lack of intelligence. <br /> <br /> That is animals (by essence?) are uninterested in tools, human type culture, rational hunting strategies, etc due to instinct and that just feeling wrong. &quot;Brother Wolf cares not for your tools, hu-man&quot;. I think you often see this in Romantic Fantasy (Robin Hobb's Farseer trilogy?) where human heroes have an animal-human mind bond.<br /> <br /> (In the real world, that's probably tough to reconcile with natural selection... but this is a magical world, where intelligence maybe has more to do with &quot;souls&quot; made by the gods than any expensive biological organ that has to be fed with huge amounts of energy, and to be useful enough to the organism's fitness that its worth doing so).<br /> <br /> Another aside; How people handle Halta's Ata-beasts may also inform these questions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T09:39:17-08:00","id":1022377,"title":"","content":"In my experience, it doesn't take magic to communicate with/use social influence on animals. Or to have animals socially influence you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T11:02:37-08:00","id":1022396,"title":"","content":"I think the answer to the folk hero animal conversationalist vs animals acting like animals might be found in other areas of the solar charmset. For example in the athletics charms where blatantly impossible feats are performed which seem to enhance things that aren't the Solar. Like graceful crane which allows a single line needle to support your weight or the ability to pull a ship against the current by swimming even though there's a whole crap tone of problems with that even if you assume a Solar who's body is infinitely fast and strong. <br /> <br /> Basically yeah animals have different intelligence than humans, although often an underestimated, except when a Solar uses his divine essence to converse with one. It doesn't make them super intelligent but it does let them transcend many of their normal limitations. Also I like the idea of finding some grain of hidden wisdom in their conversation, like speaking to a salmon about never giving up regardless of the obstacles before you, or talking to a wolf about the bonds of trust shared with your pack and the trust you must have in them etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T15:04:10-08:00","id":1022471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1021914-so-solars-can-t-speak-with-animals-anymore?p=1022311#post1022311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you are gonna have a folk/myth hero with the ability to speak with animals, I don't think &quot;hur hur, you can't get anything out of it because animals are dumb&quot; should be a big limitation.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI agree, mind; I've explained the reasons I wouldn't want powers to speak to animals in the first place, but in the case of establishing them I wouldn't want to express that in terms of &quot;the animals say useless things&quot;. I would find logical incongruities in the idea of non-sapient animals speaking congruently, but if it's a power I'll just try to do it and put those concerns aside.<br /> <br /> \u200bI suppose another way to go for a secret language of animals is something more mystical, the sense that it's not really something they converse with, but rather that they babble uncomprehending in insightful nonsense. A bird or fox might mindlessly repeat articulations in a secret language of things that they have witnessed as they go about their animal business.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}